# Copy change control

## Default rule

Do not change public-facing copy unless the user explicitly asks for copy changes.

This includes:

- headings
- body text
- program descriptions
- event descriptions
- donation language
- fundraiser language
- raffle language
- contact language
- parent-facing instructions
- safety language
- policy language
- testimonials
- quotes
- captions
- calls to action
- metadata

## Copy recommendations

If copy appears unclear, outdated, repetitive, or improvable, report it as a recommendation only.

Do not apply copy changes unless the task includes copy editing or the user approves the copy.

## Sensitive content

Do not change the meaning of:

- child safety language
- liability/policy language
- pricing
- dates
- times
- age ranges
- donation instructions
- scholarship language
- raffle/fundraiser rules
- application/registration instructions
- nonprofit or community benefit claims

## Do not invent content

Do not invent:

- dates
- prices
- program details
- staff names
- testimonials
- donor claims
- registration rules
- legal/policy language
- nonprofit status claims
- safety guarantees

If details are missing, use clearly marked placeholder text only when the user asks for a draft.